WEBVTT

00:29:59.053 --> 00:30:03.184
He extended the circle of care
and he believed we're all God's children.

00:30:03.208 --> 00:30:05.290
And he had a radical hopefulness.

00:30:05.314 --> 00:30:08.717
There was a, frankly,
religious foundation.

00:30:08.741 --> 00:30:11.983
At the same time,
he had a deep awareness of sin.

00:30:12.007 --> 00:30:14.164
There's a good book called
"A Stone of Hope,"

00:30:14.188 --> 00:30:18.224
which compares the Northern white
civil rights movement

00:30:18.248 --> 00:30:20.960
to the Southern black prophetic tradition,

00:30:20.984 --> 00:30:24.000
and the Northern white was like,
"Oh, if we just educate people,

00:30:24.024 --> 00:30:25.893
they'll see the segregation was wrong."

00:30:25.917 --> 00:30:28.088
And the Southern
prophetic tradition was like,

00:30:28.112 --> 00:30:29.364
"Sin is real in the world,

00:30:29.388 --> 00:30:32.618
and we really have to force them
to confront their own sinfulness.